  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Gaps. Fill gaps with same-suit next-rank cards, 2 only on left edge, king-right gaps are dead, and only two redeals are allowed in standard play.',
    Player: 'I need to place only the exact same-suit successor into each gap, and save redeals for stronger preserved runs.',
    objective: 'Finish with each row in same-suit order from 2 through King, leaving the four gaps immediately to the right of the Kings.',
    gameplay: 'A gap may be filled only by the card that is one rank higher and the same suit as the card immediately to its left. A gap at the far left of a row can be filled only by a 2. Gaps immediately right of a King are dead until redeal. When no legal move exists, gather all cards that are not part of correct left-to-right suit runs, redeal them into the open spaces, and continue. Standard Gaps allows two redeals, for up to three passes total.',
    keyRules: [
      'Only legal successor cards can enter a gap: same suit and exactly one rank higher than the card on the left.',
      'A left-edge gap accepts only a 2.',
      'A gap to the right of a King is dead for that pass.',
      'After all redeals are used, if any row is incomplete, the game is lost.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
